From 2b36845a051e93cbe0306509bab95caeffe8e890 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: friedger <friedger@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:53:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(oauth): silent sign-in (prompt=none) and trusted
 first-party clients

prompt=none on /api/oauth/authorize never renders a page. Signed in and the
app approved (or trusted): a code. Signed in otherwise: consent_required. Not
signed in: one round through /api/auth/oidc/start?prompt=none at the upstream
provider; its callback returns to the authorize request with a session or with
oidc_failed=<reason>, which then answers login_required.

KEYCAST_TRUSTED_CLIENTS (comma separated) skips the consent screen for those
client ids, only while they are registered clients with redirect URIs. With
OIDC_HIDE_PASSWORD_LOGIN, a trusted app's interactive request goes straight to
the upstream login instead of a page with a second sign-in button.
---
